#
# Used via -Djava.security.properties (see handler/pom.xml, argLine.javaProperties) when running the handler tests.
#
# The OpenSSL based SslEngine respects jdk.tls.disabledAlgorithms (just like the JDK implementation), but a lot of
# our tests intentionally exercise legacy protocols and cipher suites (TLSv1, TLSv1.1, RC4, 3DES, ...) that are
# disabled by default. Relax the property so these tests keep working. Tests that care about the property set it
# explicitly, see OpenSslDisabledAlgorithmsTest.
#
# SSLv3 must stay disabled: the JDK engine is used in the same JVM and tests (for example
# SslHandlerTest.testHandshakeFailedByWriteBeforeChannelActive) rely on SSLv3 handshakes failing.
jdk.tls.disabledAlgorithms=SSLv3
